## 1. Acceptance criteria

### (1) Desktop-from-disk PASS x2 with image.elf ≤80 MiB

Run 1 (clean build):
  image.elf = 12 MiB (12,628,928 bytes) ≤ 80 MiB ✓
  alpha-probe: (c) configd broadcast live (4 keys via configd_config)
  alpha-probe: (a) panel band rendered at (512,4) = 0xffe6e9ef
  alpha-probe: (b) launcher report contains hello/Utilities
  alpha-probe: PASS
  hello from package: running (from /system/bin/hello via rom_sys)

Run 2 (same build dir, fresh image):
  image.elf = 12 MiB (12,628,928 bytes) ≤ 80 MiB ✓
  alpha-probe: PASS

Both runs used: make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-desktop-disk \
  KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc RUN_OPT="--include image/disk"

### (2) ld.lib.so confirmed Tier-0 only

- grep /system/lib/: NO ld.lib.so present (CONFIRMED absent)
- system.config (XML on disk) contains 9 occurrences of ld.lib.so
  (one per dynamically linked child's route: wm, layouter, decorator,
   sponge_configd, sponge_themed, sponge_pkgd, pkg_runtime, sponge-de,
   alpha_probe — all carry ROM label_last="ld.lib.so" → parent)
- image.elf includes ld-sel4.lib.so as a Tier-0 boot module
  (auto-injected by boot_dir/sel4)

### (3) Failure channel bounded + identified

SPONGE_DISK_FAIL=1 stages a corrupted /system/init/system.config:
  <config THIS IS DELIBERATELY BROKEN XML><unclosed

Result:
  - Storage chain boots normally (ahci/part_block/vfs/rom_sys/rom_lib)
  - System init reads corrupted config → fails to start children
  - NO [init -> system -> ...] output (identifiable: success case shows
    sponge_configd/sponge_themed/sponge-de boot markers)
  - run_genode_until timeout (120s) bounds the failure
  - No silent hang — the timeout exit code is non-zero

Stage identification: storage chain OK (part_block reports GPT P3,
vfs mounts ext2, rom_sys/rom_lib start). The system init is the
failure point — it never produces child output.

### (4) Evidence file location

This file: docs/evidence/p2-desktop-disk.log

## 2. Tier-0 boot module roster (image.elf, 12 MiB)

  core-sel4.a, ld-sel4.lib.so, init, timer(hpet), report_rom,
  nitpicker, platform, acpi, pci_decode, ahci, part_block, vfs,
  cached_fs_rom (×2: rom_sys + rom_lib), vesa_fb, ps2, pc_usb_host,
  usb_hid, event_filter,
  vfs.lib.so, vfs_rump.lib.so, rump.lib.so, rump_fs.lib.so,
  en_us.chargen, special.chargen, fb.config, event_filter.config

Justification for display/input drivers in Tier 0 (§4.5 tradeoff):
  vesa_fb + nitpicker are explicitly rescue-display components (§4.7).
  ps2/usb_hid/event_filter are boot-critical (desktop unusable without
  input) and small (~3 MiB). Serving them from disk would require
  routing Platform/Dma/IRQ through the nested init — complexity for
  negligible Tier-0 savings. Total Tier-0 = 12 MiB << 80 MiB target.

## 3. /system disk layout (served by cached_fs_rom)

  /system/bin/     11 binaries (init, wm, decorator, sponge-de, ...)
  /system/lib/     37 .lib.so files (Qt6, Mesa, libc, ...) — NO ld.lib.so
  /system/init/    system.config (nested init config, XML format)
  /system/         flat: themes, tars, pkg metadata, empty config

## 4. Key design decisions

### Two cached_fs_rom instances (rom_sys + rom_lib)

cached_fs_rom resolves ROM labels via label.last_element(), which
becomes the file path relative to the vfs chroot. Binaries use
<binary name="bin/..."/> so the path includes the bin/ prefix. But
the dynamic linker requests libraries by bare name (e.g.
"libQt6Core.lib.so") with no prefix — the linker cannot be told to
add "lib/". Solution: a second cached_fs_rom (rom_lib) chrooted to
/system/lib serves .lib.so files. Routing: label_suffix=".lib.so"
→ rom_lib; everything else → rom_sys.

### §4.6 ld.lib.so rule in pkgd generator

pkgd's _generate_runtime_config now emits:
  <service name="ROM" label_last="ld.lib.so"><parent/></service>
in every generated child's <route>. This is the §4.6 convention
applied uniformly — harmless in boot-module mode, load-bearing in
disk-served mode.

### binary_prefix config option in pkgd

pkgd's <config binary_prefix="bin/"> makes the generator emit
<binary name="bin/<binary>"/> so cached_fs_rom resolves disk-served
binaries at /system/bin/<binary>.

### HID format → XML conversion for system.config

The system.config is written in HID format (Genode's indented DSL),
then converted to XML using `tool/hid format --output-xml`. This is
needed because init delivers inline configs in HID format, and
Attached_rom_dataspace::xml() (returns Xml_node) cannot parse HID.
Components reading config attributes must use .node() (handles both
XML and HID), not .xml().

### alpha_probe dual-ROM for configd broadcast

The sandbox intercepts ALL "config" ROM sessions for children with
inline configs. alpha_probe's inline <config skip_lz="yes"/> would
shadow the configd broadcast at label "config". Solution: a separate
ROM label "configd_config" (via report_rom policy) carries the
broadcast. The probe tries "configd_config" first (disk-desktop
scenario), falling back to "config" (alpha scenario).

### Flat /system/config for children without inline config

Children without an inline <config> (e.g. hello) trigger the sandbox
to open an external "config" ROM. Without a source, the denial stops
the child. A bare <config/> at /system/config satisfies these
requests so children start with empty config (non-fatal).

